pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"previous\">← Previous</th>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<th class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-label pi-secondary-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"next\">Next →</th>\n\t\t\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</thead>\n\t\n\t<tbody>\n\t<tr>\n\t\n\t\t<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"previous\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_clever_side%3F\" title=\"The clever side?\">The clever side?</a></td>\n\t\n\t\t<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"next\"><a href=\"/wiki/Cows_are_made_of_milk.\" title=\"Cows are made of milk.\">Cows are made of milk.</a></td>\n\t\n\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><i><b>9 x 7.</b></i> is the first episode of <a href=\"/wiki/Series_20\" title=\"Series 20\">Series 20</a> of <i><a href=\"/wiki/Taskmaster\" title=\"Taskmaster\">Taskmaster</a></i> and was broadcast on <a href=\"/wiki/Channel_4\" title=\"Channel 4\">Channel 4</a> on 11 September 2025. The episode was won by <a href=\"/wiki/Maisie_Adam\" title=\"Maisie Adam\">Maisie Adam</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Episode_title\">Episode title</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Episode title\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://taskmaster.fandom.com/wiki/9_x_7.?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Episode title\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Alex_Horne\" title=\"Alex Horne\">Alex Horne</a> abruptly asks <a href=\"/wiki/Greg_Davies\" title=\"Greg Davies\">Greg Davies</a> to solve \"9 x 7\" during the scoring of the <a href=\"/wiki/Do_something_behind_this_curtain_that_sounds_disgusting_but_is_actually_really_nice\" title=\"Do something behind this curtain that sounds disgusting but is actually really nice\">Do something behind this curtain that sounds disgusting but is actually really nice</a> task to calculate the total score he gave <a href=\"/wiki/Ania_Magliano\" title=\"Ania Magliano\">Ania Magliano</a>, as Greg wasn't prepared to do mental maths, the duo laugh at the prompt. The title card shows a smaller version of the target from the <a href=\"/wiki/Roll_an_object_onto_the_target\" title=\"Roll an object onto the target\">Roll an object onto the target</a> task next to a ball of ice, from the same task, and two letter tiles; one saying \"Q\" and one saying \"R\", referencing the QR code used for the <a href=\"/wiki/Honk_the_horn\" title=\"Honk the horn\">Honk the horn</a> task.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Episode_breakdown\">Episode breakdown</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Episode breakdown\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://taskmaster.fandom.com/wiki/9_x_7.?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Episode breakdown\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<div class=\"mbox\"><div class=\"mbox&#95;&#95;content\"><div class=\"mbox&#95;&#95;content&#95;&#95;wrapper\"><div class=\"mbox&#95;&#95;content&#95;&#95;header\">Spoilers!</div><div class=\"mbox&#95;&#95;content&#95;&#95;text mw-collapsible\" id=\"mw-customcollapsible-spoilers\">This section contains spoilers.</div><span class=\"mbox&#95;&#95;close mw-customtoggle-spoilers\" title=\"Dismiss\"></span></div></div></div>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"line-height: 1;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" style=\"vertical-align: top; font-family: &#39;Veteran Typewriter&#39;, monospace; font-size: 40px; font-weight: bold; text-align: left; padding: 0 5px 5px 5px;\">&#8220;\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: middle; line-height: 1.5;\"><i><a href=\"/wiki/Greg_Davies\" title=\"Greg Davies\">Greg Davies</a> returns in all his glorious majesty to rule over a brand-new series of Taskmaster. <a href=\"/wiki/Ania_Magliano\" title=\"Ania Magliano\">Ania Magliano</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Maisie_Adam\" title=\"Maisie Adam\">Maisie Adam</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Phil_Ellis\" title=\"Phil Ellis\">Phil Ellis</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Reece_Shearsmith\" title=\"Reece Shearsmith\">Reece Shearsmith</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Sanjeev_Bhaskar\" title=\"Sanjeev Bhaskar\">Sanjeev Bhaskar</a> are the latest quintet of comics who deem themselves brave enough to compete for the coveted Taskmaster trophy: Greg's golden head. As always, Greg's efficient assistant <a href=\"/wiki/Alex_Horne\" title=\"Alex Horne\">Alex Horne</a> is on hand to administer tasks involving codes, gym balls and disgusting noises.</i>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align: bottom; font-family: &#39;Veteran Typewriter&#39;, monospace; font-size: 40px; font-weight: bold; text-align: left; padding: 5px 5px -3px 5px;\">&#8221;\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align: right;\">- British Comedy Guide\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align: right;\"><small><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.comedy.co.uk/tv/taskmaster/episodes/20/1/\">[1]</a></small>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table class=\"tmtable\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"tmtableheader\">\n<th>Task\n</th>\n<th>Description\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/Ania_Magliano\" title=\"Ania Magliano\"><span style=\"color:#FFF;\">Ania Magliano</span></a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/Maisie_Adam\" title=\"Maisie Adam\"><span style=\"color:#FFF;\">Maisie Adam</span></a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/Phil_Ellis\" title=\"Phil Ellis\"><span style=\"color:#FFF;\">Phil Ellis</span></a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/Reece_Shearsmith\" title=\"Reece Shearsmith\"><span style=\"color:#FFF;\">Reece Shearsmith</span></a>\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/Sanjeev_Bhaskar\" title=\"Sanjeev Bhaskar\"><span style=\"color:#FFF;\">Sanjeev Bhaskar</span></a>\n</th></tr>\n<tr class=\"tmtablerow\">\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/A_very_soft_thing_which_would_be_most_beneficial_for_Greg_Davies\" title=\"A very soft thing which would be most beneficial for Greg Davies\">1</a>\n</td>\n<td><b>Prize:</b> A very soft thing which would be most beneficial for Greg Davies.\n</td>\n<td>3\n</td>\n<td>4\n</td>\n<td>2\n</td>\n<td><b>5</b>\n</td>\n<td>1\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"tmtablerow\">\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Honk_the_horn\" title=\"Honk the horn\">2</a>\n</td>\n<td>Honk the horn.\n</td>\n<td>3\n</td>\n<td><b>5</b>\n</td>\n<td>4\n</td>\n<td>2\n</td>\n<td>1\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"tmtablerow\">\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Roll_an_object_onto_the_target\" title=\"Roll an object onto the target\">3</a>\n</td>\n<td>Roll an object onto the target. You must release your object from behind this line. You may not move the line or target and you may not affect your object after release. You must use the first type of object you touch and can have three attempts with that type of object, and must not go within Greg's height of the target.\n</td>\n<td>1\n</td>\n<td><b>5</b>\n</td>\n<td>4\n</td>\n<td>3\n</td>\n<td>2\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"tmtablerow\">\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Do_something_behind_this_curtain_that_sounds_disgusting_but_is_actually_really_nice\" title=\"Do something behind this curtain that sounds disgusting but is actually really nice\">4</a>\n</td>\n<td>Do something behind this curtain that sounds disgusting but is actually really nice.\n</td>\n<td>3\n</td>\n<td>1\n</td>\n<td>4\n</td>\n<td>2\n</td>\n<td><b>5</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"tmtablerow\">\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/End_up_on_your_spot\" title=\"End up on your spot\">5</a>\n</td>\n<td><b>Live:</b> End up on your spot. You must obey the Taskmaster's instructions.\n</td>\n<td><b>5</b>\n</td>\n<td>4\n</td>\n<td>2\n</td>\n<td>1\n</td>\n<td>3\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"tmtabletotal\">\n<th colspan=\"2\">Total\n</th>\n<td>15\n</td>\n<td class=\"tmtablewinner\">19\n</td>\n<td>16\n</td>\n<td>13\n</td>\n<td>12\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"External_links\">External links</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: External links\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://taskmaster.fandom.com/wiki/9_x_7.?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: External links\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.channel4.com/programmes/taskmaster\"><i>9 x 7.</i> on All 4</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260920132113\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.070 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.105 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1006/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 26835/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 716/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 8/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.012/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 800499/104857600 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   63.017      1 -total\n 48.19%   30.366      1 Template:Spoilers\n 46.04%   29.010      1 Template:MessageBox\n 24.52%   15.451      1 Template: